Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 08:13:44 +0000
Subject: Patching kernel rockchip64 files drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c:
 add 164.82MHz fractional PLL rate for HDMI

The rk3568_pll_rates table lacks a 164.82 MHz entry, which is the pixel
clock required by 1920x1280@60Hz displays (e.g. ANMITE A105W01).
Without this rate, dw_hdmi_rockchip_mode_valid() rejects the mode because
clk_round_rate() on the HDMI ref clock (HPLL) returns 148.5 MHz, which
is outside the 0.1% tolerance. The pixel clock of 164820000 Hz is taken
directly from the panel's EDID Detailed Timing Descriptor (DTD), where
it is encoded as 16482 in units of 10 kHz.

This frequency cannot be expressed as an integer multiple of the 24 MHz
reference clock, but is achievable using fractional PLL mode (dsmpd=0):

  fout = 24 MHz * (54 + 15770583/2^24) / (1 * 4 * 2) = 164819999.99 Hz

Error: < 0.01 Hz (< 0.000001%)

Signed-off-by: nk-ctrl <185525803+nk-ctrl@users.noreply.github.com>
Tested-by: nk-ctrl <185525803+nk-ctrl@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c
index de350538ae5e..ed91e0951a20 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c
@@ -75,10 +75,11 @@ static struct rockchip_pll_rate_table rk3568_pll_rates[] = {
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(297000000, 2, 99, 4, 1, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(292500000, 1, 195, 4, 4, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(241500000, 2, 161, 4, 2, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(216000000, 1, 72, 4, 2, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(200000000, 1, 100, 3, 4, 1, 0),
+	RK3036_PLL_RATE(164820000, 1, 54, 4, 2, 0, 15770583),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(148500000, 1, 99, 4, 4, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(135000000, 2, 45, 4, 1, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(132000000, 1, 66, 6, 2, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(128000000, 1, 16, 3, 1, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(126400000, 1, 79, 5, 3, 1, 0),
